# Publish a post on Bluesky with its facets and up to four images, and print its URI and URL
# Validation runs before any network write. Images come from the Markdown: ![alt](path), relative to the --text-file (or to the current directory with --text)
# A post without images gets a link card from its first link (og:title, og:description, og:image). --no-embed disables it
# A page that cannot be fetched gives a warning, and the post is published without card
# --reply-to publishes a reply to any post, mine or someone else's. It takes an AT URI or a bsky.app URL, and sets the root of its thread and its parent on the record
# An unknown or invalid reference fails before anything is sent. --dry-run shows the target post
# --thread splits the Markdown on each line of three dashes, and publishes the posts one by one, each replying to the previous one
# Every post is validated before anything is sent. On a failure in the middle, the error lists the URLs already published
# With --reply-to, the first post of the thread replies to the target. Without --thread, three dashes stay in the text
# Usage:
# $ bluesky-post-create --text "Hello world"
# $ bluesky-post-create --text-file ./thread.md --thread   # One post per block between lines of ---
# $ bluesky-post-create --text-file ./thread.md --thread --dry-run   # Preview every post with its length
# $ bluesky-post-create --text-file ./post.md   # The file wins over --text
# $ bluesky-post-create --text-file ./post.md --dry-run   # Preview, uploads and writes nothing
# $ bluesky-post-create --text "See https://a.io" --no-embed   # A bare link, without card
# $ bluesky-post-create --text "Agreed" --reply-to https://bsky.app/profile/a.bsky.social/post/3k44
# $ bluesky-post-create --text "Agreed" --reply-to at://did:plc:abc/app.bsky.feed.post/3k44 --dry-run
# $ bluesky-post-create --text "Hello" --account test
setopt local_options err_return

local libDir="${functions_source[$0]:A:h:h}/__lib"
node "${libDir}/bin/bluesky-post-create.js" "$@"
